// Focused responsibility: pricing an order.
final class OrderPricer {
    private final TaxCalculator tax;

    OrderPricer(TaxCalculator tax) {
        this.tax = tax;
    }

    Money total(Money subtotal, Address address) {
        return subtotal.add(tax.calculate(subtotal, address));
    }
}
```

`OrderPricer` can be cohesive because its work is about pricing. Its coupling still depends on the size and stability of `TaxCalculator`, `Money`, and `Address`. An interface keyword alone does not settle that second question.

